hadiths[25]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3594","It was narrated that 'Amr bin Al-Harith said:""The Messenger of Allah did not leave behind a Dinar nor a Dirham"
"3595","Abu Ishaq narrated:""I heard 'Amr bin Al-Harith say: 'The Messenger of Allah did not leave behind anything except his white mule"
"3596","Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated that his father said:""I heard 'Amr bin Al-Harith say: 'I saw the Messenger of Allah and he left nothing behind except his white mule"
"3597","It was narrated from Sufyan Ath-Thawri"
"3598","A similar report was narrated from Abu Ishaq Al-Fazari"
"3599","It was narrated that Yazid -Ibn Ruzaiq- said:""Ibn 'Awn narrated to us"
"3600","It was narrated from Bishr"
"3601","It was narrated from Azhar As-Samman"
"3602","It was narrated that Anas said:""When this Verse was revealed -'By no means shall you attain Al Birr (piety"
"3603","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""Umar said to the Prophet: 'The one hundred shares that I acquired in Khaibar -I have never acquired any wealth that I like more than that"
"3604","It was narrated that 'Umar"
"3605","It was narrated that 'Umar said:""I asked the Messenger of Allah about some land of mine in Thamgh. He said: 'Freeze it and donate its fruits"
"3606","Al-Ahnaf said:""I came to Al-Madinah"
"3607","It was narrated that Al-Ahnaf bin Qais said:""We set out for Hajj"
"3608","It was narrated that Thumamah bin Hazn Al-Qushairi said:""I was present at the house when 'Uthman looked out over them and said: 'I adjure you by Allah and by Islam"
"3609","It was narrated from Abu Salamah bin 'Abdur-Rahman that 'Uthman looked out over them when they besieged him and said:""By Allah"
"3610","It was narrated that 'Abdur-Rahman Al-Sulami said:""When 'Uthman was besieged in his house"
"3611","It was narrated that Abu Hurairah said:""A man came to the Prophet and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3612","It was narrated that 'Abdullah said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'For whom among you is the wealth of his heirs dearer to him than his own wealth?' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"3613","It was narrated from Mutarrif"
"3614","Abu Habibah At-Ta'i said:""A man made a will leaving some Dinars (to be spent) in the cause of Allah. Abu Ad-Darda' was asked about that"
"3615","It was narrated that Ibn 'Umar said:""The Messenger of Allah said: 'It is not befitting for a Muslim who has anything concerning which a will should be made"
"3616","It was narrated from Ibn 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah said:""It is not befitting for a Muslim who has anything concerning which a will should be made"
"3617","(The same) was narrated from Ibn 'Awn"
"3618","It was narrated from 'Abdullah bin 'Umar that the Prophet said:""It is not befitting for a Muslim to abide for three nights without having his will with him."" 'Abdullah bin 'Umar said: ""Since I heard this from the Messenger of Allah"